.TH PSGetModelAtIndex 3 2024-01-03 "PsyC 0.9.4" "PsyC Library Functions Manual"

.SH NAME
\fBPSGetModelAtIndex\fR

.SH LIBRARY
PsyC (-lpsyc)

.SH SYNOPSIS

.B
#include <psyc/psyc.h>

.I
PSModel  *
.br
\fBPSGetModelAtIndex\fR(\fIPSModel *entrypoint\fR, \fIint index\fR)
.SH DESCRIPTION
Get the model at \fIindex\fR in the multi-model chain that contains the model \fIentrypoint\fR. If \fIindex\fR is negative, it will be counted from the end of the model chain (ie. -1 is the last model, or tail,  of the chain).  

.SH RETURN VALUES
The model or \fINULL\fR if:

.RS 4
\[bu] \fIentrypoint\fR is \fINULL\fR
.br

\[bu] the model chain is broken
.br

\[bu] \fIindex\fR is out of bounds.
.br
.RE

.SH SEE ALSO
psyc(1), PSAddModel(3), PSModelChainContains(3), PSModelChainHead(3), PSModelChainLength(3), PSModelChainTail(3)
